From: Lee Ford <472320+leeford@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:06:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] Skip the gdi32 D3DKMTQueryAdapterInfo hook on ARM64EC

clang-cl compiles hkD3DKMTQueryAdapterInfo to a single BRK #1 for
ARM64EC, so the first call through the detour raises an illegal
instruction. OptiScaler's own GetDriverStore (from checkGpuInfo) makes
that call as DXVK starts, which crashes every D3D11 game on launch.

The hook only spoofs HAGS and the AMD FSR 4 GPU check, which do not
apply on Adreno, so leave gdi32 unhooked on ARM64EC until the codegen
problem is understood.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 OptiScaler/hooks/Gdi32_Hooks.h | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/OptiScaler/hooks/Gdi32_Hooks.h b/OptiScaler/hooks/Gdi32_Hooks.h
index a6d0a02..d8bf493 100644
--- a/OptiScaler/hooks/Gdi32_Hooks.h
+++ b/OptiScaler/hooks/Gdi32_Hooks.h
@@ -106,6 +106,15 @@ static void hookGdi32()
 {
     LOG_FUNC();
 
+#if defined(_M_ARM64EC)
+    // clang-cl compiles hkD3DKMTQueryAdapterInfo to a lone trap (BRK #1) for
+    // ARM64EC, so the first D3DKMTQueryAdapterInfo call (DXVK, or our own
+    // GetDriverStore) kills the game. The hook only spoofs HAGS and the AMD
+    // FSR 4 GPU check, neither of which applies on Adreno.
+    LOG_INFO("Skipping D3DKMTQueryAdapterInfo hook on ARM64EC");
+    return;
+#endif
+
     o_D3DKMTQueryAdapterInfo =
         reinterpret_cast<PFN_D3DKMTQueryAdapterInfo>(DetourFindFunction("gdi32.dll", "D3DKMTQueryAdapterInfo"));
 
